-- CK-20: a rigid met more than once inside one derived shape is ONE
-- `missing_where_constraint` per rigid and method at the comparison, and two
-- rigids are two (checker-v2.md §9.2's rigid row, as built by R6a's review,
-- F4). On 68186fa v1 checks all three clean (CK-20); R6a's first round said
-- the same clause once per occurrence.
f : a, a -> Bool
f x y =
    ( x, x ) == ( y, y )


g : a, b -> Bool
g x y =
    ( x, y ) == ( x, y )


h : a -> Bool
h x =
    { p = x, q = x, r = x } < { p = x, q = x, r = x }
